      "sha": "abaf2cf38d6576c5c2b31a3dc2bb06469660de1e",
      "message": "✨ Improve GC measurements (#16)\n\n* ✨ Observe natural GC during sampling\n\nTiming samples now run back to back after one initial collection, so natural\nGC stays in the measured cost. A single observer records GC events during\nsampling, and heap estimation moves to a separate diagnostic pass after timing.\n\nReports show observed GC cost per iteration with its share of sampling time,\ncollection frequency, the longest pause, and major collections. Older saved\nresults keep their forced collection estimates.\n\n* ✅ Test terminal behavior instead of TUI layout\n\nShared screen tests cover navigation, resize, cleanup after render errors,\nCtrl+C, and escape stripping. The comparison view keeps a check that\nbenchmarks without statistics never show stale ones.\n\n* 📝 Add a GC example\n\nBenchmarks grouped by garbage pressure: low, short-lived, and retained. They\nrun small camera and scene routines with no dependencies, so the gc and\ngc max columns have something to show.\n\n* 💡 Disallow property comments in types\n\n* 📝 Simplify readme",
      "url": "https://github.com/pmndrs/labs/commit/abaf2cf38d6576c5c2b31a3dc2bb06469660de1e"
    }
  ],
  "scope": "Read-only upstream source context. The current default branch package identifies itself as 0.10.0; this does not authenticate an npm 0.10.0 artifact or any other repository's installed version. No upgrade or measurement was run. Adaptive warmup and moving forced collections out of each timing sample are upstream changes, not evidence that either caused or prevents the saved 113 ms Glyph block. All current fixed20 comparisons remain on pinned patched 0.9.0."
